From f359ad12a39b918fe88bee57dfd3df503c73a716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:01:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): [daveey] refuse a bare vendor model id on
 OpenRouter/Nous before any request; API worker logs carry the session tag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Kanban worker (MacBook, 2026-10-27 22:00 PT) resolved provider=openrouter
while keeping the bare id claude-opus-5-5, and its only request died with
HTTP 400 "claude-opus-5-5 is not a valid model ID" — an error naming neither
the route nor why it was taken. The pin-without-provider route itself was
fixed by 9c943cbd2f; nothing stopped any other route (auto config, fallback,
cron, CLI) from doing the same.

- agent/model_provider_guard.py: after the client is built (the provider is
  final only then), a bare id with a known vendor (claude-*, gpt-*, ...) on
  openrouter/nous raises ModelProviderMismatchError, logged at WARNING, naming
  provider, base URL, model and route (pinned/fallback/auto) and suggesting
  vendor/model or --provider <vendor>. Ids with "/" and unknown house ids pass.
  agent.model_provider_guard: false turns it off.
- chat_completion_helpers._context_thread_target now carries the thread-local
  session id into the API worker thread, so "Streaming failed before delivery"
  reaches errors.log tagged [<sid>] and the errors signal can name the session.
- test_provider_parity's Nous fixture used bare "gpt-5" (not a Nous id; every
  Nous catalogue entry is vendor/model); it now uses openai/gpt-5.

Self-heal agent-1572c64e24.
